Slide 1: CES Phase II Reporting Approach
Current Assessment

Phase II reporting requirements were reviewed and validated with the business team.

Key observations:

Most reports are direct replacements of existing Crystal Reports
Business preference is for simple operational reporting
Primary output requirement is PDF reports, with Excel export capability
Limited demand for dashboards, advanced analytics, or self-service BI
Current CES data structure is optimized for transactional reporting rather than interactive analytics
Fit-to-Need Analysis
Business Need	Telerik / HTML5	Power BI
Crystal Report replacement	✅ Strong fit	⚠️ Moderate fit
PDF generation	✅ Strong fit	✅ Capable
Excel export	✅ Strong fit	✅ Capable
Operational reporting	✅ Strong fit	⚠️ More than required
Complexity	✅ Low	❌ Higher

Conclusion: Current requirements align more closely with a traditional reporting platform than a business intelligence platform.

Slide 2: Recommendation
Recommended Approach

Leverage .NET Core HTML5 / Telerik Reporting within CES

Benefits:

✅ Faster delivery using existing CES technology stack

✅ Report output closely matches current Crystal Reports

✅ Native PDF and Excel export capabilities

✅ Lower implementation and support complexity

✅ Reduced training and maintenance effort

✅ Reuse existing development expertise and infrastructure

Strategic View

Power BI remains a strong future option if CES reporting evolves toward:

Executive dashboards
KPI monitoring
Trend analysis
Self-service analytics

For current Phase II requirements, Telerik Reporting provides the simplest, most cost-effective, and lowest-risk solution.

Recommendation

Proceed with .NET Core HTML5 / Telerik Reporting as the primary CES Phase II reporting platform.

We are open to leadership feedback, alternative perspectives, and recommendations before finalizing the reporting architecture and implementation approach.
